  "409": {
    "inputs": {
      "value": "Extreme telephoto shot on a roughly 1500mm lens, flat compressed perspective that stacks the open grassland plain and the low blue-grey mountain ridge directly behind her.\n\nA young woman in pale teal-blue and cream traditional robes walks straight toward the camera from far away, starting as a small full-body figure and growing steadily larger at a calm, unhurried pace; her brown leather belt with a sheathed sword, the bow across her back and her long black hair half tied in a topknot stay clearly readable even at that distance.\n\nA force-6-to-7 gale blows in from frame left the whole time, whipping the wide hem of her cream outer robe into a long streaming banner that flaps in repeated waves and lifting her teal skirt, while her long hair and loose strands are driven hard toward frame right, strands sweeping across her face.\n\nAbout a third of the way through, a thick horizontal gust of yellow sand blows across the middle of the frame at her chest and waist height, briefly veiling her before streaming off to the right; airborne grains and drifting dust fill the air throughout. Each footstep kicks up dust from the dry grass.\n\nThe camera stays locked off with only a faint long-lens tremor in the wind, keeping her centered, and she ends up close to the lens in exactly the stance, framing, hair shape, clothing and warm side light of the reference image. Photorealistic, cinematic, shallow depth of field, natural daylight, single continuous take, 8 seconds."
